{"autose": "session-start", "role": "judge", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "label": "r0-requirements-2", "attempt": 0, "prompt": "Acceptance criteria:\n- AC-FR-001-1: Given the extensions `toc` and `attr_list` and the issue's example document (`# Guide`, `## Contents {: .no-toc }`, `[TOC]`, `## Install`, `## Usage`), when it is converted, then the output contains `href=\"#guide\"`, `href=\"#install\"` and `href=\"#usage\"` and does not contain `href=\"#contents\"`.\n- AC-FR-001-2: Given the same document, when it is converted, then `md.toc` contains `href=\"#install\"` and does not contain `Contents`.\n- AC-FR-001-3: Given the same document with `{: .no-toc }` removed from the \"Contents\" heading, when it is converted, then the output contains `href=\"#contents\"`.\n- AC-FR-002-1: Given the issue's example document with `toc` and `attr_list`, when it is converted, then the output contains `id=\"contents\"` on the `h2` element whose text is `Contents`.\n- AC-FR-002-2: Given two headings `## Contents {: .no-toc }` and `## Contents` in one document, when it is converted, then the two headings have different `id` values and neither is empty.\n- AC-FR-002-3: Given `## Contents {: .no-toc #custom }`, when it is converted, then the heading has `id=\"custom\"`.\n- AC-FR-003-1: Given the issue's example document with `toc` and `attr_list`, when it is converted, then `md.toc_tokens` has one top-level entry with `id` equal to `guide`, and its `children` list holds entries with `id` equal to `install` and `usage`, in that order.\n- AC-FR-003-2: Given the same document, when it is converted, then no entry anywhere in `md.toc_tokens` has `id` equal to `contents`.\n- AC-FR-003-3: Given the extension `toc` only and the document `# A` followed by a blank line and `## B`, when it is converted, then `md.toc_tokens` equals `[{'level': 1, 'id': 'a', 'name': 'A', 'html': 'A', 'data-toc-label': '', 'children': [{'level': 2, 'id': 'b', 'name': 'B', 'html': 'B', 'data-toc-label': '', 'child